me_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01MK33UQrny4AMHkviZeVuM2", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 56268, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01MK33UQrny4AMHkviZeVuM2", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 58769, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_015Gezot4UKGZbXYnWKpjFXC", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 59069, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_015Gezot4UKGZbXYnWKpjFXC", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 59069, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_015Gezot4UKGZbXYnWKpjFXC", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 63758, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all regions and healthy again, and SEV2 incident INC-0001 is open.\n\n**Rollback:**\n- v2.3.0 was the most recent healthy release. Both later releases, v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1, were unhealthy.\n- The first rollback stopped partway with an orchestrator error. Only us-east moved to v2.3.0, and us-west and eu-west stayed on v2.3.1.\n- I ran the rollback again and it finished. All three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) are now on v2.3.0.\n- The service reports healthy, and the error rate dropped from about 18% to about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident:**\n- The request to open the incident timed out. Before retrying, I checked the incident list and found it had been created anyway, so I didn't open a second one and page on-call twice.\n- INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api) is open. It describes the bad v2.3.1 deploy, the rollback that stopped partway, the second attempt that worked and the current health.\n- It lists two follow-ups: find out why v2.3.1 failed before redeploying it, and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01KwukinaWX4GUCfgTo5Nu7h", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01RBCp1qh7Cim3tQqRtDVDBf", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Going by sequence number, v2.3.0 (seq 1) is the most recent healthy release. Both later releases, v2.3.1-rc (seq 2) and v2.3.1 (seq 3), are unhealthy.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01AQs1fqaTubtbktJy6dTvYt", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_013MXvKiQVmxJWdP6FYtWSHZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollout stopped partway, so only us-east is on v2.3.0. A rollback to a known-healthy version is safe to repeat, so I'll retry it once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01PcvjM8udUT4VZtn89sdSS8", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01FurtHhsBdAVqp4UPmrpf7o", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01V4jhcTdA3EKxWidviqCHFH", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01MK33UQrny4AMHkviZeVuM2", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 was failing health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. Deploy history shows v2.3.0 as the most recent healthy release (v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1 were both unhealthy). The first rollback attempt to v2.3.0 failed partway with an orchestrator error after us-east, leaving regions on mixed versions (us-east v2.3.0, us-west/eu-west v2.3.1). A second rollback attempt completed. All three regions now run v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failures before redeploying, and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The request timed out, so the incident may or may not exist. I'll check before retrying so I don't page twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_015Gezot4UKGZbXYnWKpjFXC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all regions and healthy again, and SEV2 incident INC-0001 is open.\n\n**Rollback:**\n- v2.3.0 was the most recent healthy release. Both later releases, v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1, were unhealthy.\n- The first rollback stopped partway with an orchestrator error. Only us-east moved to v2.3.0, and us-west and eu-west stayed on v2.3.1.\n- I ran the rollback again and it finished. All three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) are now on v2.3.0.\n- The service reports healthy, and the error rate dropped from about 18% to about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident:**\n- The request to open the incident timed out. Before retrying, I checked the incident list and found it had been created anyway, so I didn't open a second one and page on-call twice.\n- INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api) is open. It describes the bad v2.3.1 deploy, the rollback that stopped partway, the second attempt that worked and the current health.\n- It lists two follow-ups: find out why v2.3.1 failed before redeploying it, and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "type": "text"}]}]}